3. Hosted-Service Prohibition

You may not use VidDub, or any modified version or derivative of VidDub,
to provide or support a Hosted Service. You may not expose VidDub
functionality, model inference, or a substantially similar derivative to third
parties through an API, website, application, bot, platform, cloud endpoint,
managed deployment, or other remote-access service.

This prohibition applies whether access is public or private, paid or free,
and whether VidDub is the primary service or a component of another
product. A separate written license from the licensor is required for any such
use.

For clarity, an individual may charge for completed videos or other outputs,
or perform project-based creative work, provided that the individual operates
VidDub themselves and does not give a client or other third party access to
the model or its inference functionality.

